fr:mainmatter.fr:p:
For a category \mathcal {C}, a subobject classifier is an object Ω together
with a global element true : 1 → Ω such that ∀ A ∈  \mathcal {C} . ∀ s : S ↣ A. ∃!     χ_s : A → Ω.
\usepackage {tikz-cd} \usepackage {unicode-math}
     \begin {tikzcd}
        S  \ar [d, rightarrowtail, "s"'] \ar [r] \ar [dr, phantom, " \lrcorner ", very near start]  & 1  \ar [d, rightarrowtail, "true"]  \\ 
        A  \ar [r, "χ_s"'] & Ω
     \end {tikzcd}

is a pullback square.

For a category \mathcal {C}, a subobject classifier is an object Ω together
with a global element true : 1 → Ω such that ∀ A ∈  \mathcal {C} . ∀ s : S ↣ A. ∃!     χ_s : A → Ω.
