is a pullback square.

            "The class of types is closed under the inductive clauses:

1, N and Ω are types ('basic' types);



                    if A and B are types, so are A×B and \mathcal {P} A"

            "The class of terms is freely generated from certain basic terms by
            certain operations including the following… and is closed under certain operations.


                    [for each type A, there are countably many variables
                    x_1^A, x_2^A, …;]


* is a term of type 1;



                    if a is a term of type A and b is a term of type
                    B, then ⟨a,b⟩ is a term of type A×B;



                    if a is a term of type A and α is a term of type
                    \mathcal {P} a, then a ∈ α is a term of type Ω;



                    if ϕ(x) is a term of type Ω (possibly containing the
                    free variable x of type A), then \{ x ∈ A | ϕ(x) \}
                    is a term of type \mathcal {P} A not containing a free occurrence of
                    x;


0 is a term of type N;



                    if n is a term of type N so is Sn;


⊤ and ⊥ are terms of type Ω;



                    if p and q are terms of type Ω, so are p∧q,
                    p∨q, p⟹q;



                    if ϕ(x) is a term of type Ω (possibly containing the
                    free variable x of type A), then ∀_{x∈A}ϕ(x) and
                    ∃_{x∈A}ϕ(x) are terms of type Ω not containing free
                    occurrences of x.
                "

